# NOTE: do not add `allow-scripts=...` here. npm >= 12 (the version in Vercel's
# build image) rejects that key in a project-scoped install with EALLOWSCRIPTS
# and fails the whole deploy. Install scripts are approved per package in the
# `allowScripts` field of package.json instead, and nothing in this project
# needs one: esbuild ships its binary through optional platform packages, so
# `npm test` and `npm run register` work with its postinstall blocked.
